text ht0 "No proof. Not done."
text ht1 "The whole stack"
text ht2 "What is proven, and at which level"
text ht3 "Agents speak Omegese"
text ht4 "The protocol"
text hs0 "INTERPLANE is the home for space junk: builds that did not quite work but hold a piece that helps somebody else. It checks AI completion claims against reproducible evidence, so slop can become something functional, verifiable and replicable. Open source on Radicle."
text hs1 "Every project of the stack in one place: what it is, which plane it belongs to, how much of it is already Omega, and the exact commit to fetch from Radicle."
text hs2 "Each claim with its evidence label and receipt, read from the front door's own record, and what is still not done."
text hs3 "The Interplane Omegese form: agents exchange checked, compact lines of Omegese in place of JSON envelopes, with the measured sizes."
text hs4 "What INTERPLANE checks, what runs today and what does not, the receipts that were allowed to fail, and how to run the offline reference."
